ng it is and do  them a favor tell them you're only  giving them certain sections rather than  them getting frustrated at you probably  sit there for such a long presentation I  just hope that they were awake through  all of it because that's a problem Terry  we heard testimony from an alleged  victim someone who apparently survived  an attack testified about her encounter  with Ortiz how do think her testimony is  going to impact the jury impact this  case oh it's going to be a huge impact  on this case  surviving  Vic you better believe that that jury is  listening to every word that she is  saying they are listening to what he did  to her he picked her up he threw her in  the van he put a gun to her head and she  got out of that car and she was able to  escape she got help from a state trooper  and I think the jury is thinking this  must have happened exactly the same way  with the other women and so she was able  to tell the story for everyone a key  strategic move on the part of the  prosecution they put her up the first  day and had that impact I think that  they were looking for even though she  did admit that she did prostitution and  drugs I don't think the jury is going to  hold that against her well as we talk  about this unbelievable testimony and as  the Juan David Ortiz trial was underway  on Thursday there was other shocking  news and Associate associate district  attorney quit that's right according to  local television stations in Texas in  Texas Joshua Davila posted on Facebook  quote I have officially left the Webb  County District Attorney's office that  is the most unprofessional and toxic  workplace I have ever had to deal with I  do not recommend it Davila was actually  in the courtroom for the first three  days of the trial even questioning  Witnesses on the stand the District  Attorney's Office wouldn't comment other  than to say that his resignation  wouldn't impact the trial  [Music]  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

